(3. Bank / hold / exception controls) Tj
T*
(Bank records and hold events are immutable. Their order is \(event_on, sequence\).) Tj
T*
(Choose latest eligible CHANGE per vendor even if its account is not verified.) Tj
T*
(The latest CHANGE must have status ACTIVE. BANK_UNVERIFIED unless a VERIFY) Tj
T*
(references that exact CHANGE ref AND account,) Tj
T*
(has status VERIFIED, role TREASURY_REVIEWER, different actor_id from) Tj
T*
(the CHANGE maker, and is strictly later in \(event_on, sequence\). Same timestamps) Tj
T*
(require sequence comparison. Old account verification never verifies a newer change.) Tj
T*
(bank_account_ref is the latest CHANGE account even on HOLD; blank only if none exists.) Tj
T*
(ACTIVE_HOLD: any eligible OPEN has no later CLOSE for the SAME business key AND) Tj
T*
(hold_id, by role AP_CONTROLLER/RISK_MANAGER. Other roles or hold IDs cannot close it.) Tj
T*
(A later OPEN reopens a hold; earlier closes cannot close that new OPEN.) Tj
T*
(Exception approvals are in BUL-TR-01. Only role CFO may waive) Tj
T*
(PO_MISMATCH, RECEIPT_SHORT, and only reasons explicitly named on that approval.) Tj
